tracted archives only if cheap. Do not recursively extract all nested blobs.\n5. Write `$output/summary.txt` listing offsets, sizes, commands, and artifact paths. Once summary.txt is non-empty, stop immediately and print `AGENTFLOW_SKILL_DONE`.\n\nHard constraints:\n- Do not use `binwalk -eM` or `binwalk -e -M`.\n- Do not recursively copy or expand the full `$output/binwalk_extract` tree.\n- Do not perform vulnerability analysis, disassembly, or broad reverse engineering.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778250986113},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the task. I need to:\n\n1. Input: `/home/icsl/sothoth/13-secflow-service/image_build/secflow-app-firmware-unpacker/targets/demo2/S6730_V200R024C00SPC500.cc`\n2. Output: `/home/icsl/sothoth/13-secflow-service/image_build/secflow-app-firmware-unpacker/unpacked-demo2-skill-rerun-unified/S6730_V200R024C00SPC500.cc/output`\n\nThe skill guidance says to extract specific components at known offsets:\n- main xz SquashFS: offset 41668, size 123581704\n- gzip SquashFS 1: offset 123648804, size 8111913\n- gzip SquashFS 2: offset 135199940, size 7491332\n- Linux uImage kernel: offset 142746844, size 2524096\n- uImage ramdisk: offset 145271292, size 9589941\n\nI need to:\n1. Create output directories\n2. Run binwalk\n3. Extract the components with dd using large block sizes\n4. Write summary.txt\n5. Print AGENTFLOW_SKILL_DONE\n\nLet me start.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll follow the skill guidance to extract the Huawei S6730 .cc firmware. Let me start by creating the output directories and running binwalk."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fb7478e06f296b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p \"/home/icsl/sothoth/13-secflow-service/image_build/secflow-app-firmware-unpacker/unpacked-demo2-skill-rerun-unified/S6730_V200R024C00SPC500.cc/output/artifacts\" \"/home/icsl/sothoth/13-secflow-service/image_build/secflow-app-firmware-u